=======================================================
SHOPGRAPH TAXONOMY
==================

The taxonomy is:

```
Common Name
    ↓
Sub-Category
    ↓
Category
```

Category Manager is authoritative for:

```
Sub-Category -> Category
```

Purchase History is authoritative/supporting evidence for:

```
Product
Common Name
Sub-Category
Store
SKU
historical purchase information
```

=======================================================
ONLY MODIFY CATEGORY = NA
=========================

This is a critical safety rule.

Only Category Manager rows whose Category is blank or NA may be changed.

Existing non-NA Category assignments are authoritative.

NEVER allow Ollama to overwrite, rename, normalize, reorganize, or otherwise modify an existing non-NA Category.

Before writing anything, capture the original Category Manager state.

Immediately before writing, verify again that every proposed target still has Category blank/NA.

If a target no longer has blank/NA Category, refuse to overwrite it.

=======================================================
DETERMINISTIC COMPLETION FIRST
==============================

Before calling Ollama, attempt deterministic completion.

Build the existing authoritative:

```
Sub-Category -> Category
```

mapping from all valid non-NA Category Manager rows.

If the same normalized Sub-Category already has exactly one authoritative Category elsewhere, reuse that Category without asking Ollama.

Do not invent deterministic mappings from semantic similarity.

Only exact/normalized identity mappings should bypass Ollama.

Any genuinely unresolved Category = NA row should be sent to Ollama.

