```
shopgraph_category_completion_prompt.txt
```

Do not redesign the taxonomy rules.

The local Ollama prompt must preserve the important behavior of the existing external-AI prompt:

1. Existing non-NA Category assignments teach the broad taxonomy.

2. Only Category = NA rows are targets.

3. Existing Category names should be reused exactly when appropriate.

4. Products/Common Names belonging to the target Sub-Category should be used as evidence.

5. Purchase History should be used as supporting evidence when useful.

6. Prefer an existing broad Category when it genuinely fits.

7. Do not create synonymous or near-duplicate Categories.

8. A new Category may be created only when the Sub-Category belongs to a materially different purchasing domain not represented adequately by the existing taxonomy.

9. New Categories should be:
   concise
   human-readable
   broad
   reusable
   consistent with existing naming style

10. Do not assume everything belongs to Food.

11. Use NA only when evidence is genuinely insufficient.

12. Never modify existing non-NA Category assignments.

